WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.734
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.067
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.501
Well, guys, we are right in the
middle of the holiday season,

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:14.267
and I saw that Instacart
is now offering

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.968
same-day delivery
for Christmas trees.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:21.100
So remember to tip,
because your delivery guy

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.000
definitely has an ax.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.667
Yeah, wow.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:31.100
Of course, it's Instacart, so
get ready for a text that says,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.133
"They're out of Christmas trees.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.267
Is Pepsi okay?"

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:36.234
And you go, "Pepsi?
That's not even --"

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:40.000
Yep, Christmas trees
on Instacart.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.801
It's a beautiful
new family tradition

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.934
of gathering around papa
until he swipes right

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:46.200
on the perfect balsam fir.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.767
"Dad's getting his phone out.
Come on, let's gather up."

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:52.968
I don't want someone else
picking out my Christmas tree.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.868
I don't even like someone else
picking out my cantaloupe.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.200
I was like, "Oh,
you thought that was ripe?

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.467
Didn't you knock on it?"

00:00:58.467 --> 00:00:59.467
Is that what you do with
a cantaloupe?

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:00.834
Do you knock on it?

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.267
-You got to thwap the end.
You smell it. You know.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.334
-Certain things I just knock on

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.400
and think I know
what I'm talking about.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.601
Do you knock on a pineapple?
That does nothing.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:09.200
You peel the leaf of
a pineapple.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.334
-You pull the leaf.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.834
-Watermelon I knock on,
of course.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.501
That goes without saying.
-Knock on wood.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.100
-I knock on watermelons
I don't even buy.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.033
I just go up and go,
"Hey, what's up?"

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.234
-Fill it with vodka.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:21.567
Did you guys see this?

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:24.367
New York just passed a law that
makes all gift cards

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.667
purchased in the state
valid for at least nine years.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.934
-Ooh!

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.834
-You know you got someone
the perfect gift card

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.901
when it takes them 8 1/2 years
to use it.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:36.734
"Well, you like
Home Depot, so..."

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.133
8 1/2 -- Yeah.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.267
They're good for nine years,
although I'm not quite sure

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.767
what to do with a valid gift
card from Borders Bookstore.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:43.968
What am I doing?
What am I doing?

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:45.601
Find me a Borders.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:46.901
Let's get to some news.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.701
Due to a rise in
COVID, RSV, and flu cases,

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:52.334
New York City health officials
issued an advisory

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:55.868
urging people to wear masks
again.

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:57.534
I think they're getting
tired of these announcements,

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.300
'cause this one felt a little
more casual than the rest.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.367
Take a look at this.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:04.667
That's...
-Wow.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.601
-That was fast.
♪♪

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.167
That's it?

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.667
That was fast.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:15.334
That's right -- New York City
is experiencing

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.701
high levels of
COVID, flu, and RSV,

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:20.501
and health officials are
calling it a "tridemic."

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.868
-Aw, come on, man.
We can do better than that.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.400
-What's that, Tariq?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.300
-I said we can come up with
a better name than a "tridemic."

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.300
That's so clunky.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.501
-Yeah, you're right.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.834
"Tridemic" doesn't even
rhyme with anything.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:31.868
What are you thinking?

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.434
-Um, the three-sles.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.334
-That's good.

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:40.367
Scarlet three-ver.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:43.334
-Hepa-thri-tis.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:46.567
-Gono-three-a.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:50.267
-The thrice-capades.

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:51.667
-The thrice is right.

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.300
-Trip-slip.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.534
-Fuzzy triple.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:56.567
-Mm...

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:59.200
uh, "Three Strains and a Baby."

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.334
-"Three Strains and a Rabies."

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:04.701
-Once, twice, three
types of achy.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:07.167
-The Tri Guys.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.434
-We can just call it
"Three's Company."

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.934
-How about "All I Want for
Christmas is Achoo"?

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:14.868
-Rocking around
a Christmas three.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.300
-Oh. The tres race.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.434
-Ooh! The tres force.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.868
-Left without a tres.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:25.767
-All aboard the flu-flu strain
choo-choo train.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:29.868
-That's it.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:32.200
That's the one. That's it.
Tariq Trotter got it right.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.434
[ Dinging ]
That's it, buddy.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:35.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.968
Well, guys,
Elon Musk is still on his

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.000
"trying to make
people upset" tour.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.267
And Elon is being slammed
for a tweet

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.734
he posted yesterday that said...

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:56.234
Fauci was like, "Yep,
much like a Tesla battery,

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:59.300
Elon's on fire."

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.567
Yeah. You could tell Fauci
wasn't having it

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.501
because he wrote back,
"Congrats on making Twitter

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:06.634
the Johnson &amp; Johnson vaccine
of social media."

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.367
Thank you.

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.901
Meanwhile, Elon also said that
Twitter's character limit

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:21.534
for tweets is going to increase
from 280 to 4,000.

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:24.834
People are like,
"4,000 characters?

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:28.067
At that point, I may as well get
my news from the news."

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.834
Switching gears,
King Charles just released

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:35.100
the first royal
Christmas card of his reign.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.367
Ready for it? Here it is.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.901
"Wishing you a very happy
Christmas and New Year."

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:41.634
It has the same
emotional feeling

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.868
as a holiday card
from your dentist.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.100
"I can see through this."

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.367
Seriously, the love and emotion
just flows from that guy's pen.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.400
Are there budget cuts
at Buckingham Palace?

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.734
Is that --
Is Elon firing everyone

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:57.033
in the card division over there?

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.234
Well, here's some big news.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.934
The other day, a lot of people
were surprised to

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:04.033
see Ben Affleck getting coffee
at Starbucks.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.968
-Oh!

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.868
-Ben Affleck was
drinking Starbucks,

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.501
and it didn't take long for
Dunkin' to respond.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:12.534
Watch this.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:14.267
-Well, well.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.534
You think you're better than us,
Benedict Affleck?

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.801
You think you're wicked smart
going to Starbucks,

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:23.601
sipping $6 drinks like
the freaking King of England.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.234
Enjoy your foam in a dome,
you L.A. jabron.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:27.634
Just go ahead and go.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.734
Tom Brady left us,
and we're fine.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:33.334
We still got Matt Damon
and a half-dozen Wahlbergs.

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:34.601
We'll bounce back,

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:37.367
even if we feel the way
Bill Belichick looks.

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:43.667
-Oh! That's so sad. Wow.

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:45.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.667
-Moving.
-No, you know ben.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:50.801
This is Dunkin'.
He's Dunkin' all the way.

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:52.033
-Yeah, come on.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:54.167
-And, finally, we have
exactly five shows left

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:56.000
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.734
that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:05:57.734 --> 00:06:01.567
It's time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters."

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:03.868
-♪ 12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:09.167
♪ Five days left ♪

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:14.334
-That's right -- every show
between now and Christmas,

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:16.400
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.200
an mm-mm-mm Christmas sweater

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.000
from the "Countdown to
Christmas Cabinet."

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.067
Since there are five shows left,
let's open door number 5.

00:06:25.067 --> 00:06:26.100
Where do we go?
Where do we go?

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.033
-Right here.
-Alright, go for it, bud.

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:30.334
Whenever you're ready.
Oh, my gosh!

00:06:30.334 --> 00:06:32.767
Wow! I don't know what that is.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:33.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:37.434
Is that a sweater?

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:39.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.334
I don't know what the heck --
-Turn it around?

00:06:44.334 --> 00:06:46.200
-Yeah.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.501
That's the back of it there.

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:50.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:51.501
-Wow.

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:53.234
Alright. Wow!
-Wow.

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:55.834
-Oh, my gosh. This is heavy.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.734
Alright, now let's see who's
going home -- Wow!

00:06:57.734 --> 00:06:59.133
This is 100 pounds.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.667
Let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:01.734
Everyone look at your
seat number, okay?

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:04.133
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.734
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:07:05.734 --> 00:07:06.868
[ Drumroll ]
Who wants this sweater?

00:07:06.868 --> 00:07:08.868
This is a...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:16.234
314!

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:19.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:21.534
Come on down.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.467
Come on!

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:30.000
It's getting heavy.

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:35.234
Come on!

00:07:35.234 --> 00:07:37.200
Hey, come on,
we got a show to do.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.934
Come on, get over here.

00:07:38.934 --> 00:07:41.300
Here, go on over there.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.701
Gosh, this sweater's heavy.

00:07:42.701 --> 00:07:44.667
You take your time
with that one.

00:07:44.667 --> 00:07:46.300
Gosh. Welcome.
-Oh, sorry.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.467
-Thank you for coming.
Thank you for being here.

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.634
What is your name?
-Marcella.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.234
-Marcella, where are you from?
-California.

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:54.634
-Hey!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:57.834
Marcella, this is perfect
for California.

00:07:57.834 --> 00:07:58.901
-Yeah.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:01.567
-Everyone in L.A.
will be wearing these.

00:08:01.567 --> 00:08:03.067
Do you have anything
like this at home?

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:05.834
-Nope.
-Oh! Nothing even close?

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:07.167
-Uh, no.
-Yeah.

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:08.968
Marcella, would you try this
on for us tonight?

00:08:08.968 --> 00:08:10.067
-Yeah.
-Alright, cool.

00:08:10.067 --> 00:08:11.868
Roots, can I get some music?
♪♪

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:14.334
We need some help here.

00:08:14.334 --> 00:08:16.501
Alright, good luck.

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:17.901
I feel your head.

00:08:17.901 --> 00:08:19.434
I feel your head in there.
Okay, good.

00:08:19.434 --> 00:08:21.634
Marcel-- Oh! Can you breathe?

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:23.534
-Yeah.
-Yes, you're good. Alright.

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.200
Sorry.
-I'm, like, nervous.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.667
-No, that's alright.
Oh, yeah, good, Marcella.

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.767
Yeah, gorgeous.
-Oh!

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:31.033
-No, this is perfect.
Marcella, turn around.

00:08:31.033 --> 00:08:32.200
This is good.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:35.968 --> 00:08:39.667
Oh, my gosh.
That is unbelievably gorgeous.

00:08:39.667 --> 00:08:41.667
Beautiful.
Thank you so much, Marcella.

00:08:41.667 --> 00:08:43.501
Congratulations.
Thank you very much.

00:08:43.501 --> 00:08:46.934
-I just had an
ugly Christmas sweater, um...

00:08:46.934 --> 00:08:49.667
-You just had an
ugly Christmas sweater party?

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:50.801
-Party.
-Yeah.

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:52.000
-And it's too late.
-Yeah, too late now.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.133
But you got to go back.

00:08:53.133 --> 00:08:55.634
But you have this to go to
the next one.

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:57.667
Have another party next week.
Thank you very much.

00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:59.601
Congratulations. Thank you.
Good job!

00:08:59.601 --> 00:09:02.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:09:02.634 --> 00:09:05.334
-Can I have a hug?
-Yeah, of course.

00:09:05.334 --> 00:09:07.200
-Thank you.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:16.200
-Fur and glitter and everything.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.834
Well done, pal.
You rocked that out.

00:09:20.868 --> 00:09:23.667
Guys, you know what?

00:09:23.667 --> 00:09:25.400
I'm not done.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:32.300
How come only one person
gets to win something, huh?

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:34.567 --> 00:09:36.767
Let's take this
to the next level!

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:38.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:40.968
It's time for "Tonight Show
Stocking Stuffers"!

00:09:40.968 --> 00:09:42.067
Here we go!

00:09:42.067 --> 00:09:45.100
♪ It's "The Tonight Show" ♪

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.767
♪ It's "The Tonight Show" ♪

00:09:46.767 --> 00:09:48.200
-♪ Stocking stuffers ♪

00:09:48.267 --> 00:09:52.000
-♪ Stocking stuffers ♪

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.167
-Now, there is no need to check
under your seats for this one.

00:09:56.167 --> 00:09:58.033
Every night
until Christmas break,

00:09:58.033 --> 00:09:59.834
we're giving away
an awesome gift

00:09:59.834 --> 00:10:03.634
to every single person
in our studio audience.

00:10:03.634 --> 00:10:06.234
You guys excited?
You guys ready?

00:10:06.234 --> 00:10:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:07.834 --> 00:10:12.667
You guys want to see what you're
going to take home tonight?

00:10:12.667 --> 00:10:14.834
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:10:14.834 --> 00:10:19.601
